Y465_REASON='The source first chooses x with u*(1_Z)=u*(x), then chooses y in the image of j_* from the closed complement Z′. Exactness of K(Z′) --j_*→ K(X) --u*→ K(U) identifies the needed supported correction as y=cl(O_Z)−x; the same identity holds after tensoring every group and map with Q. For η=Σa_α[O_{Z″_α}] in K(Z′), the exact direct-image map sends it to y=Σa_α[j_*O_{Z″_α}], with each support inside Z′⊂Z and avoiding the generic point z. Thus each support has codimension>k and the induction applies to y. Adding y to the displayed cl(O_Z)−y∈Fil^k gives cl(O_Z)∈Fil^k, exactly the desired conclusion. The printed x assertion fails in an instance with no coefficient ambiguity: take X=P¹ over a field and Z one rational point, and choose U=X because Z is already a regular Cartier divisor. Then Z′ is empty, u=Id, x=cl(O_Z), and y=0. Euler characteristic sends x to1, so x is nonzero, whereas every combination of sheaf classes on the empty Z′ is0. For the second printed assertion put h=1−[O(−1)]=cl(O_Z). The projective-bundle presentation gives K(P¹)=Z[h]/(h²). Its total gamma operation is γ_t(h)=1/(1−ht)=1+ht, and for any rank-zero element nh it is (1−ht)^(−n)=1+nht. Hence every gamma generator of degree≥2 and every product of two positive-degree generators is0, so Fil²_gamma K(P¹)_Q=0; x=h remains nonzero after rationalization because χ_Q(h)=1. This also directly refutes the final printed x∈Fil². The two y substitutions restore the exact localization argument, with no change to its hypotheses or surrounding x used for the lift.'
