RATLIFT465=own(465,'integral lift symbols following a rational filtration membership','x∈Fil^kK(X), y∈j_*K(Z′), after u*(1_Z)∈Fil^kK(U)_Q','the same printed integral group symbols','Retain the author’s body; record the complete rational construction and the unresolved stronger integral choice.','unresolved_mathematical_argument','Both full main strips and witness476 show the lack of Q on the filtered surjection and on the following x and y memberships. The source explicitly mentions the tensorized localization sequence immediately before this argument. Tensoring its maps with Q gives j_{*,Q}=j_*⊗id_Q and u^*_Q=u*⊗id_Q; exactness follows because Q is a flat Z-module. Tensoring the displayed surjection of filtration groups gives Fil^kK(X)_Q→Fil^kK(U)_Q. Thus the displayed rational target u*(1_Z) has a rational lift x_Q. Then δ=cl(O_Z)⊗1−x_Q lies in ker(u^*_Q)=im(j_{*,Q}), so choose η_Q with j_{*,Q}(η_Q)=δ and put y_Q=δ. The rationally extended supported-class decomposition and induction give y_Q∈Fil^{k+1}, while cl(O_Z)⊗1−y_Q=x_Q∈Fil^k, completing the stated rational conclusion. This explicit construction establishes rational choices. It does not by itself establish integral choices for these particular geometric classes; no counterexample excluding such integral choices or uniquely determined omitted source phrase has been established here. Therefore no Q is inserted into this body passage and no stronger mathematical assertion is invented. The two independently disproved x-for-y slips are corrected separately.','retained with unresolved integral-lift strength');OWN[-1]['misprint']=False;OWN[-1]['additional_evidence']=['scan/SGA6_witness_300dpi.djvu#page=476']
